---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<div class="academy-hero not-content">
	<div class="academy-hero__copy">
		<span class="eyebrow">A beginner-first systems field guide</span>
		<h1>Learn what games are <em>really</em> doing.</h1>
		<p>Memory, assembly, graphics, packets, and reverse engineering—explained in plain English, then explored with small buildable programs.</p>
		<div class="hero-actions">
			<a class="button button--primary hero-resume" data-resume-link data-resume-base={base} href={`${base}/pages/1/01/`} hidden>
				<span data-resume-label>Continue reading</span> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
				<small class="hero-resume__detail" data-resume-detail></small>
			</a>
			<a class="button button--primary" data-resume-start href={`${base}/pages/1/01/`}>Start lesson one <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
			<a class="button button--ghost" href="#course-map">See the course map</a>
			<a class="button button--ghost" href={`${base}/glossary/`}>Browse the glossary</a>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="academy-hero__terminal" aria-label="A tiny typed-code example">
		<div class="terminal-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>first_lab.rs</b></div>
		<pre><code><span class="code-dim">// Data has a type.</span>
<span class="code-keyword">let</span> mut gold: u32 = 40;

<span class="code-dim">// We can observe a change.</span>
gold += 10;

assert_eq!(gold, 50);</code></pre>
		<div class="terminal-status"><span>✓ clear</span><span>✓ safe</span><span>✓ yours</span></div>
	</div>
</div>

<script>
	import { mountResume } from '../../scripts/resume-reading.js';
	mountResume();
</script>

<style is:global>
	.hero-resume[hidden] { display: none; }
	.hero-resume__detail { display: block; max-width: 22rem; margin-top: 0.15rem; font-size: 0.75em; font-weight: 400; opacity: 0.9; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
